// The model lives under a `namespace`, so its runtime identity is `demo.storage.Todo` — NOT `Todo`.
// That is the whole point of this example: the repository is keyed by that qualified name, and
// nothing here writes it out by hand.
//
// `rank` is an `int` rather than a `bool` on purpose. SQLite has no boolean storage class and reads
// one back as 0/1, so a `bool` field would fail to decode from a SQLite row (`expected bool, found
// JSON number`) and every row would come back unmapped — a driver read-back fact, unrelated to the
// name resolution this example is about. Postgres has a real `boolean` and maps it fine.
@derive(Serialize<Json>, Deserialize<Json>)
pub struct Todo {
    pub id: int
    pub title: string
    pub rank: int
}
